  "raw": " party \"could have done without\" entering into an inspection agreement with the Eskom-owned entity which seemingly lends credibility to its US$75 billion black empowerment targeted investment drive, dubbed the Eskom Accelerated Black Economic Empowerment (EABE) Owned Projects Programme.\n\nEarlier in May, the Eskom board recommended to the Eskom shareholders that they should have supported the Eskom Accelerated Black Economic Empowerment (EABE) Owned Projects Programme as \"a strategic direction to bring about near full transformation of the Eskom Group by 2021\" and would \"build and progressively disinvest into existing and legacy assets\". There are no further details on the Eskom Accelerated Black Economic Empowerment (EABE) Owned Projects Programme as there has been no public presentation.\n\nThe facility, in an inspection agreement obtained by Business Maverick, was placed in a survey taken by the Eskom CEO, Brian Molefe and the Eskom's Finance Director,",
  "serialized": "party \"could have done without\" entering into an inspection agreement with the Eskom-owned entity which seemingly lends credibility to its US$75 billion black empowerment targeted investment drive, dubbed the Eskom Accelerated Black Economic Empowerment (EABE) Owned Projects Programme. Earlier in May, the Eskom board recommended to the Eskom shareholders that they should have supported the Eskom Accelerated Black Economic Empowerment (EABE) Owned Projects Programme as \"a strategic direction to bring about near full transformation of the Eskom Group by 2021\" and would \"build and progressively disinvest into existing and legacy assets\". There are no further details on the Eskom Accelerated Black Economic Empowerment (EABE) Owned Projects Programme as there has been no public presentation. The facility, in an inspection agreement obtained by Business Maverick, was placed in a survey taken by the Eskom CEO, Brian Molefe and the Eskom's Finance Director,",
